[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   Step 085 -- DES independent resident-cohort audit.
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   Every resident-signature test so far runs on the JPL SBDB catalogue:
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   one database, one orbit-determination pipeline, discoveries drawn
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   overwhelmingly from northern surveys.  The Dark Energy Survey TNO
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   release (Bernardinelli et al. 2022, ApJS 258, 41; data release
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   bernardinelli/des_tno_catalog) is the largest single-survey TNO
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   catalogue with uniform selection -- 814 objects discovered in a
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   contiguous 5000 deg^2 of southern sky with orbits fitted
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   independently of SBDB.  Its detached subset is therefore the only
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   public independent resident cohort on which the registered axis can
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   be scored.
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   This step:
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   1. downloads the DES orbit table to data/raw/des/ with the same
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   provenance record used by steps 001-004;
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   2. selects the detached cohort (a > 150, q > 30) -- the 16 objects
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   Bernardinelli et al. themselves reported as "consistent with the
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   null hypothesis of azimuthal isotropy" (their null is the 2-D
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   azimuthal distribution; the pre-declared directional cap is a
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   different, more powerful statistic);
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   3. scores the cohort against the registered P1 axis: in-cap fraction
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   versus uniform (1/3), versus the step_054 footprint baseline
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   (~0.42), versus the registered mixture prediction (0.59), and
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   versus the cohort's own designation-derived footprint baseline
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   (the same half-month opposition-longitude model as steps 014/054/
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   084) -- the honest comparison, since DES opposition fields sit in
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   the axis sector;
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   4. cross-matches the cohort against the SBDB secure sample to (a)
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   measure the sample overlap -- how independent the DES cohort
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   actually is in membership -- and (b) measure the resident-side
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   inter-catalogue floor: the per-object |Delta varpi| between the
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   DES and SBDB orbit determinations of the same bodies, the
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   resident analogue of the step_079 comet cross-fitter audit.
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   Outputs
[2026-09-20 12:41:56 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 085]   results/step_b50_des_resident.json
